.TH rt 1 "September 2024" "rt 1.0" "Remote Terminal Control"
.SH NAME
rt \- Remote terminal client for accessing your computer via SSH and web interfaces

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rt
.RB [\-l
.RB [\fIDIRECTORY\fR]]
.RB [\-h]
.RB [\-s
.IR SOCKET ]
.RB [\-p
.IR PASSWORD ]
.RB [\-\-help]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rt
is a secure remote terminal client that connects to a
.B rtd
daemon running on your machine. It provides multiple connection methods:
.IP \(bu 2
Interactive SSH terminal access through a Cloudflare tunnel
.IP \(bu 2
Browser-based web terminal for monitoring and hibernation control
.IP \(bu 2
Sandboxed directory access for running Claude Code on other machines

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-l \fR[\fIDIRECTORY\fR]
Start an interactive remote shell session. If
.I DIRECTORY
is provided, the session is restricted to that directory (sandbox mode).
If no directory is given, the current working directory is used.
.TP
.B \-h
Access the hibernation control panel via web interface. When in hibernation mode,
the remote will refuse all new requests and close existing sessions.
.TP
.B \-s \fISOCKET\fR
Specify the Unix socket path for daemon communication
.RB (default:
.IR /tmp/rt.sock ).
.TP
.B \-p \fIPASSWORD\fR
Provide the authentication password. Required for all connections.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display help message and exit.

.SH USAGE EXAMPLES
.TP
Start a remote shell in the current directory:
.B rt \-l \-p mypassword

.TP
Start a remote shell in a specific directory (sandbox mode):
.B rt \-l /path/to/project \-p mypassword

.TP
Access hibernation control panel:
.B rt \-h \-p mypassword

.SH SECURITY NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Always set a strong password with
.B rtd
.IP \(bu 2
Failed authentication attempts trigger exponential backoff and temporary lockout
.IP \(bu 2
All traffic should be protected by SSH or Cloudflare tunnel encryption
.IP \(bu 2
Sandbox mode restricts filesystem access to the specified directory only

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rtd (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR chroot (2)

.SH AUTHOR
Implemented as part of the PUtils remote access suite.
